# Cursor-Primary Night Worker Rule

- For a cursor-primary config, Cursor/Grok is the preferred worker and local Qwen is fallback.
- v1 does not spawn the Cursor CLI unattended. Unresolved or unavailable Cursor providers must fall back to local Qwen.
- Resolve any future CLI model id with `agent --list-models`; never guess it.
- Keep a fresh coding session per NIGHT_SAFE task.
- The deterministic Night Orchestrator remains in control of scope, tests, retries, PASS/BLOCKED and reporting.
- Do not use `--force` or `--yolo` to bypass unattended safety.
- Morning reports must record which provider performed each task.